 parts the problem here  is he couldn't get everybody  only five villains were willing to help  him engage in his plan to take on  spider-man and of course those five guys  were vulcan mysterio electro sandman and  craven the hunter and so what you saw  over the course of this story at least  in the initial beginnings anyway peter  parker was was kind of losing his powers  a lot of this was predicated on the idea  of his internal guilt over the death of  uncle ben how that basically haunted him  and how it changed his life it's the one  great failing that peter parker sees  himself as consistently having in more  recent years it's also the death of gwen  stacy but nonetheless the fact that he  was struggling mentally in this way  meant the time was perfect for dr  octopus to strike and so what he did is  he basically enlisted the other members  of the six and then in turn what they  ended up doing was one kidnapping betty  brandt and on may of course betty brandt  basically being the love interest of  peter parker at the time not really his  true love you know she wasn't gonna be  the girl that he was gonna go on to  marry of course the intention was for it  to be gwen stacy jerry conway killed her  off in the 70s and it became mary jane  watson but she was his first kind of  girlfriend right the first real  girlfriend that peter parker had the  other thing is that in order to defeat  spider-man they had to break away from  the status quo the way things had always  worked previously at least for the most  part when peter parker faced off against  these different members of the sinister  six is that when a fight broke out he  would usually lure them to a location  where spider-man stood the best possible  chance of winning right very much a  playbook out of sun tzu's the art of war  doctor octopus sought to turn that on  its head and lure spider-man to a place  where the villains stood the best chance  of winning and so that's why when the  whole thing pops off and s