nt may has no real clue what's  going on now in reality they've been  kidnapped by the sinister six as a means  to basically lure spider-man in and then  try to find a way to destroy them but  the goal of otto octavius was not to  kill aunt may or betty brandt in order  to defeat peter parker the goal was to  defeat peter parker and to use them as a  means to get to him and so again while  the fight takes place between each  member of the sinister six and then  ultimately leads to a fight between  spider-man and doctor octopus which of  course spider-man's able to successfully  overcome and then saves aunt may and  betty brant and the day kind of goes on  this had a huge amount of of beefing up  for peter parker in the spider-man  mythos and the reason was this it was no  secret at the time that spider-man was  exceedingly intelligent right the peter  parker was a highly intelligent young  man the biggest problem that he had here  was differentiating between how many  instances peter parker came out on top  because of a combination of his spider  sense and his abilities in comparison to  using his brain what this story did is  it solidified this idea that with peter  parker facing off against these various  villains in landscapes and areas that  are the most suitable for them by all  standards of measurement they should win  but peter parker using a combination of  his abilities as well as his head  allowed him to gain the upper hand and  defeat these guys despite overcoming  overwhelming odds i mean quite literally  it was a gauntlet right it was one fight  after the other just one fight after  another after another after another and  so following sinister six one thing that  i do want to point out here this was  only ever designed to be a one-off  that's the reason why there's a 20-year  gap between this original sinister six  appearance in 1964 and the return of the  sinister six in 1990. now in reality if  you guys are really interested we can  talk about the di